  "id": "rumination-syndrome",
  "term": "Rumination Syndrome",
  "definition": "Rumination syndrome is a gastrointestinal disorder in which recently eaten food repeatedly and effortlessly comes back up from the stomach into the mouth soon after eating. It is different from GERD and vomiting, can occur beyond infancy, and is associated with functional digestive problems as well as psychiatric conditions such as anxiety and depression.",
